// γ-verification ADVERSARY baseline fixture for indexed-sub-instantiation §7 δ.
// Premise the prover missed: δ's deliverable covers the forall/exists QUANTIFIER
// EXPRESSIONS ("`Int` element type"), not just the forall statement — and the
// expression path has its OWN Range<Int> rejection site with DIFFERENT diagnostic
// text: crates/reify-compiler/src/expr.rs:5216 emits
// "cannot iterate over non-collection type 'Range<Int>' in forall/exists: expected List<_> or Set<_>"
// (note "in forall/exists" vs the statement path's "in forall" from
// forall_elaborate.rs:274). A δ acceptance test keyed only on the statement
// diagnostic string would not cover this site. This fixture also exercises the
// `exists` keyword, absent from both prover fixtures despite the leaf title.
// Expected: `reify check` exits 1; stderr contains the "in forall/exists" text
// (verified 2026-07-25 against target/debug/reify built same day: exit 1, the
// diagnostic fires once per quantifier expression — twice for this fixture).
// NOTE: after δ lands this fixture's expectation inverts (range domains become
// accepted, binder typed Int); the δ task owns retiring/repurposing it.
structure def Rig {
    let all_ok = forall i in 0..4 : i >= 0
    let any_ok = exists i in 0..4 : i >= 0
}
